{"descriptionModels":[{"description":"Prerequisite: Variant Human, Balthazar Origin (Your stats can\u0027t be less than 10 each one)\nSpecial Note: This feat is given upon character creation.\n\nYou are a Baltazar, a Primordial, a fragment of time and space, you are one and many. You are Legion. As pompous and grandiose as this may sound, you are basically a regular human, with some significant changes:\n\n- You can\u0027t age and you are immune to any effects that would cause you to age magically.\n\n- Your alignment can\u0027t change except in levels that are multiples of seven (1st, 7th and 14th in a regular campaign)\n\n- Your soul can\u0027t be captured by any means, nor shaped. When you die, you can\u0027t be resurrected by any means short of a Wish spell (if the DM allows it) as your soul is broken into thousands of pieces and dispersed through the cosmic void between planes.\n\nYou can choose the nature of your soul (Your Variant Human feat with some additional mechanics)\n\n- Dark Soul: The basic soul of most Baltazars. You choose an Spellcasting feat or Draconic Gift. Instead of having a relationship to some weird lineage, a Dragon Gift or a traumatic event, this represents an untamed dark power in the very core of your soul. The Sorcerer class is always available for you, no matter your stats, and if you choose the Shadow Magic origin, you have aditional Sorcery Points equal to half your proficiency bonus (rounded up)\n\n- Pure Soul: The pure, new, untainted soul of many Era of Chaos Baltazars. You choose any feat, which represents your specialization or special nature. You can\u0027t be compelled, magically or via a Charisma check to do anything that goes against your alignment. However, you suffer from a problem related to demons. If your Wisdom score is less than 18, whenever you see or feel a demon or a creature with Tanaar\u0027i blood (Abyssal or Infernal), you make a Wisdom saving throw, with a DC equal to 8 + your Proficiency Bonus. If you fail it, the DC augments by one for subsequent saving throws. If you succeed, it drops by one. When you fail this check, you enter a frenzy, and you must act under the following mechanics until the frenzy ends:\n\n* You must use your actions, bonus actions, and reactions in your turn to atack and harm the source of your frenzy. This means that if you have choices for each one and one of them is harmful, you must always choose the one that would harm the source of your frenzy. Otherwise, you use an option that would get closer to the source of your frenzy, or one to defend yourself.\n\n* You must pursue the source of your frenzy at all cost. This means that if you have no ranged atacks able to hit the target, and the source is within 120 feet of you, you must use your movement to get closer to it.\n\n* You know the position of the source as long as it is within 120 feet of you.\n\n* You move with swift and uncanny speed. You are always under the effects of the Dodge action whenever you are within 5 feet of the source. You can take the Dash action as a bonus action while the frenzy lasts.\n\n* You are atacks are vicious and meant to butcher. Whenever you deal damage with an unarmed strike or weapon atack, you deal additional damage equal to your proficiency bonus. Your critical range is increased by 1.\n\n* If you killed the source of your frenzy while within 30 feet of it, you can eat it\u0027s soul, preventing it from returning to it\u0027s home plane, and regaining hit points equal to twice your level.\n\nAt the DM\u0027s discretion, you can tailor this curse as it better fits your character or campaign, such as choosing not to harm certain creatures after certain tests have been passed and eliminating any, if not all of the drawbacks and benefits of the frenzy state. The frenzy ends when the character doesn\u0027t feel any living demon creature in a 120 feet range, and it isn\u0027t seing one.\n\n- Broken Soul: Yours a very rare kind of soul among the Baltazars. Broken souls are those of formerly deceased Baltazars that somehow have regained most fragments of their soul and reincarnated into a new Baltazar. You retain the memories of reincarnations chosen by you, giving you insights about certain things. You don\u0027t get to choose a feat. Instead, you gain the following benefits:\n\n* Your soul is flexible and easy to rebuild, as it is now as glass fragments guided by one will. You loose the common feature related to souls of all Baltazars. If you die, spells that can bring you to life again don\u0027t have a cost in special components if cast upon your character. Additionally, if you know any of these spells, once per long rest you can cast one  upon yourself when you die as a reaction.\n\n* If you die in a campaign and you aren’t able to resurrect, this character can be considered the same for another campaign, as your fragments travel the Multiverse waiting for reincarnate again.\n\n* You know the Magic Missile spell, and you can cast it at will at a level equal to your proficiency bonus. You can also control the number of missiles that appear, up to a minimum of one and a maximum given by the spell level. The damage inflicted is necrotic instead of force. However, whenever you cast the spell, you loose 5 hit points for every missile that damages a target. This missiles represent fragments of your soul that you guide to pierce through the soul of your enemies.\n\n- Soul of the Betrayer: Yours is the soul of the Betrayer, the Ultra-Baltazar, the second born of your kind, the eternal one that bears the sins of the many. Your path is hard to walk through. But at the end you are the one who remains, silently watching as eons pass. The Soul of the Betrayer is a story bending and high challenge soul, so decide with your DM and the other players if it\u0027s appropriate for the campaign and tailor your backstory accordingly. You get to choose 2 Feats instead of one. However, the regular CR of the monsters you and the party encounters increase by an amount equal to your proficiency bonus. You also have the features of the Broken Soul origin, with the exception of the Magic Missile feature.","level":1}],"id":"Custom5e1d8eba-7829-4f8f-a918-43cd57aad1cd","isFeature":false,"jsonType":"feat","level":1,"name":"Balthazar Forever [SM]","notes":"","type":"Feat"}